Upstream:      OrcaSlicer (github.com/SoftFever/OrcaSlicer): src/slic3r/GUI/Plater.cpp.
               On main the width tracking has moved to AuiMgr::track_docked_size
               in src/slic3r/GUI/AuiMgr.cpp, still with no minimum.
Upstreamable:  yes
How:           A PR against main that gives the sidebar pane a minimum width and
               has track_docked_size ignore widths below it. No issue or PR
               filed yet.
Written:       2026-11-26, against OrcaSlicer 2.4.2
Last checked:  2026-11-26: unfixed on main
Remove when:   the OrcaSlicer release that nixpkgs packages keeps the docked
               sidebar at or above its minimum width
Applied by:    modules/desktop/orca-slicer.nix

The Prepare tab's sidebar can get stuck a few pixels wide.

The sidebar is an AUI pane with no minimum size, and SetDockSizeConstraint(1, 1)
lets the left dock shrink to almost nothing. An idle handler copies the pane's
current width into best_size on every idle tick, SavePerspective() writes that
to window_layout in OrcaSlicer.conf on exit, and LoadPerspective() restores it
on the next start. One moment at a tiny width (a sash drag, or the window
briefly configured very small) gets saved, and the sidebar comes back at that
width every time: talos had "bestw=18" in window_layout.

The patch gives the pane a minimum width of 39 em (Sidebar's own minimum and
its default width), applies it again after LoadPerspective (the saved layout's
minw=-1 replaces it), widens a saved width below the minimum, and has the idle
handler skip widths below the minimum.

--- a/src/slic3r/GUI/Plater.cpp
+++ b/src/slic3r/GUI/Plater.cpp
@@ -5054,6 +5054,7 @@
                                    .CloseButton(false)
                                    .TopDockable(false)
                                    .BottomDockable(false)
+                                   .MinSize(wxSize(39 * wxGetApp().em_unit(), -1))
                                    .BestSize(wxSize(39 * wxGetApp().em_unit(), 90 * wxGetApp().em_unit())));
 
     auto* panel_sizer = new wxBoxSizer(wxHORIZONTAL);
@@ -5085,13 +5086,20 @@
                 BOOST_LOG_TRIVIAL(info) << "Removed floating AUI state from saved window layout for Wayland";
             }
 
+            // The saved layout carries its own minw=-1, which replaces the minimum set above, and may carry a
+            // width saved while the sidebar was squeezed narrower than that minimum.
+            const int sidebar_min_width = 39 * wxGetApp().em_unit();
+            sidebar.MinSize(wxSize(sidebar_min_width, -1));
+            if (sidebar.best_size.GetWidth() < sidebar_min_width)
+                sidebar.BestSize(sidebar_min_width, sidebar.best_size.GetHeight());
+
             sidebar_layout.is_collapsed = !sidebar.IsShown();
         }
 
         // Keep tracking the current sidebar size, by storing it using `best_size`, which will be stored
         // in the config and re-applied when the app is opened again.
         this->sidebar->Bind(wxEVT_IDLE, [&sidebar, this](wxIdleEvent& e) {
-            if (sidebar.IsShown() && sidebar.IsDocked() && sidebar.rect.GetWidth() > 0) {
+            if (sidebar.IsShown() && sidebar.IsDocked() && sidebar.rect.GetWidth() >= 39 * wxGetApp().em_unit()) {
                 sidebar.BestSize(sidebar.rect.GetWidth(), sidebar.best_size.GetHeight());
             }
             e.Skip();
